n well says: \"How does any one love the man to whom he gives food and drink for the very purpose of heaping coals of fire upon his head, if `coals of fire 0' in this place dignify some heavy punishment?\" The meaning is: thou shalt by returning good for evil, bring the evildoer to shame and remorse. This course will be the dictate of Christian love because it will tend to reveal the man's wrong-doing to himself, induce repentance for it and lead him to forsake it. The repentance of Saul is an example (1 Sam. xxiv. 17). \"And Saul lifted up his voice and wept. And he said: thou art more righteous than I: for thou hast rendered unto me good, whereas I have rendered unto thee evil.\"-G. B. S.","note":"Stellenangabe der Ausgabe (englische Zählung, umgerechnet)"},{"id":"848418663f37","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.hom_rom","w":"chrysostomus.hom_rom","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":28,"p":[7,7],"r":[19,10],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"1 Sam. xix. 10"},{"id":"617f4361fb56","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.hom_rom","w":"chrysostomus.hom_rom","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":29,"p":[23,23],"r":[19,5],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"1 Sam. xix. 5"},{"id":"47d1004a53fb","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.hom_rom","w":"chrysostomus.hom_rom","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":29,"p":[23,23],"r":[12,23],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"1 Sam. xii. 23"},{"id":"dff2dc0d453a","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.hom_1co","w":"chrysostomus.hom_1co","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":33,"p":[12,12],"r":[20,30],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"1 Samuel chapter 20, verse 30"},{"id":"0501f2becd62","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.hom_2co","w":"chrysostomus.hom_2co","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":7,"p":[36,36],"r":[16,12],"k":"quotation","m":"editionCitation","c":"high","cited":"1 Samuel chapter 16, verse 12"},{"id":"8ea9373e7324","v":"npnf.chrysostomus.hom_2co","w":"chrysostomus.hom_2co","a":"johannes_chrysostomus","s":15,"p":[17,17],"r":[12,